    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties are honoured to present Seacliff, an exceptional waterfront residence occupying an extraordinary position on the dramatic East Cork coastline.\r\nSet directly above the shoreline in the peaceful coastal enclave of Guileen, this unique home enjoys uninterrupted panoramic views across the Irish Sea, with the ever-changing seascape forming the backdrop to everyday life. From sunrise over the water to passing yachts and fishing boats navigating the harbour, Seacliff offers a front-row seat to one of Ireland's most captivating coastal settings.\r\nOriginally constructed in the mid-19th century and thoughtfully extended and upgraded in recent years, the property successfully combines the charm and character of a traditional coastal cottage with the comforts and efficiency of contemporary living. Extending to approximately 92.5 sq. m. (996 sq. ft.), the accommodation is beautifully presented throughout and designed to maximise both natural light and the spectacular sea views.\r\nThe property's outdoor spaces are equally impressive. An elevated deck with glass balustrading overlooks the shoreline below, while a remarkable roof terrace provides a private vantage point from which to enjoy the coastline stretching towards Roches Point, Cork Harbour and beyond.\r\nDespite its wonderfully secluded setting, Seacliff is conveniently located just minutes from Whitegate, Roches Point and Aghada, with Midleton and Cork City easily accessible. Sailing, kayaking, swimming, paddleboarding, sea angling and coastal walks are all available from the doorstep, creating a lifestyle opportunity rarely found on the market.\r\nWhether as a permanent residence, luxury holiday home or coastal retreat, Seacliff represents a truly unique opportunity to acquire a home in one of East Cork's most breathtaking waterfront locations.\r\nAccommodation: Kitchen/ Living/ Dining Room, 3 Bedrooms (1 en-suite) and Bathroom\r\n\r\nGuide Price: €525,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Porch:\tA welcoming entrance porch leading directly into the main living accommodation.\r\nKitchen/ \r\nLiving/ \r\nDining Room: The heart of the home is an impressive open-plan living space featuring a \r\nvaulted ceiling which enhances the sense of volume and light throughout.\r\nThe living area centres around a feature solid-fuel stove, while the \r\ncontemporary shaker-style kitchen is fitted with an excellent range of units\r\nand integrated appliances including double oven, hob, microwave, \r\ndishwasher and fridge/freezer. Large windows frame views towards the \r\ncoastline, while tiled flooring flows seamlessly throughout the space.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: \tA double bedroom positioned to the rear of the property with tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:  \tA second bedroom positioned to the rear of the property with tiled flooring. \r\n\r\nBathroom: \tComprising W.C., wash hand basin and shower. Fully tiled.\r\n1st Floor:\r\nBedroom 3 / \r\nMain Bedroom: A generous double bedroom positioned on the upper floor with wooden flooring and a built-in slide robe.\r\n\r\nEn-suite:             Comprising W.C., wash hand basin and electric shower. Fully tiled.\r\n\t\t\r\nServices:   \tBio-cycle. \tMains water.\tO.F.C.H.\tFibre broadband.\r\n\r\nOutside: \r\nApproached via a private laneway, Seacliff occupies an enviable waterfront position with uninterrupted views across the Irish Sea.\r\nThe front garden has been carefully designed to maximise the property's stunning coastal outlook and features a contemporary elevated deck with glass balustrading, creating the perfect setting for outdoor dining and entertaining.\r\nTo the rear, a sheltered courtyard provides an additional private outdoor space, while a separate garden area and gravelled parking area offer ample parking for multiple vehicles.\r\nA fully insulated Steeltech shed provides valuable additional space and offers potential for a variety of uses including a home office, hobby room or storage facility (subject to any necessary consents).\r\nThe property's dramatic coastal setting, combined with its multiple outdoor living spaces, creates an exceptional lifestyle opportunity rarely available on the East Cork property market."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tExceptional waterfront residence with uninterrupted sea views \r\n•\tDirectly overlooking the Irish Sea \r\n•\tElevated rear terrace \r\n•\tElevated sea-view deck with glass balustrading \r\n•\tOriginally built in 1850\r\n•\tExtended and upgraded in 2022 \r\n•\tBER: B\tBER No.: 119462943\r\n•\tApprox. 92.5 sq. m. / 996 sq. ft. \r\n•\tFibre broadband available \r\n•\tFeature solid-fuel stove \r\n•\tContemporary shaker-style fitted kitchen \r\n•\tThree bedrooms, including principal bedroom with en-suite \r\n•\tPrivate courtyard and garden areas \r\n•\tFully insulated Steeltech shed\r\n•\tAmple private parking \r\n•\tWalking distance to the shoreline \r\n•\tMinutes from Whitegate, Roches Point and Cork Harbour \r\n•\tLess than 30 minutes from Midleton \r\n•\tRare coastal lifestyle property"
